---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';

const path = '/use-cases/product-launch';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'use-cases/product-launch');
const desc = description(site, 'use-cases/product-launch');
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a href="/use-cases" class="link text-sm font-bold">← All use cases</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Coordinate Shopify product launches</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-slate-700">Launch operations connect a published product, eligible markets, stock allocation and the promises made to a waitlist.</p>
    <article class="prose-shopify card mt-12 max-w-4xl p-8">
      <h2>Define launch readiness</h2>
      <p>Write a release checklist for product visibility, purchasable variants, destination availability, pricing and support readiness. A scheduled message should not itself determine that the product is live. Name the person who can delay the announcement when merchandising is not ready.</p>
      <h2>Distinguish interest from allocation</h2>
      <p>A waitlist records interest unless the store has explicitly promised a reservation or queue position. State which applies in signup and launch copy. Early access requires a working access mechanism and an agreed end time; membership in a VIP segment alone is not access control.</p>
      <h2>Protect variant and market relevance</h2>
      <p>Match interest to the requested size or variant where that information exists. Decide whether to offer alternatives when it sells out. Stop stale cart reminders that still promise launch stock, and update landing copy when availability changes. Do not claim scarcity from a campaign timer alone.</p>
      <h2>Choose tools around the release plan</h2>
      <p>A capture tool, messaging tool and storefront access mechanism have different jobs. Request a demonstration of the handoff among them, including exports of waitlist preferences and purchase exclusions. Compare the maintenance burden of these integrations rather than assuming an app name proves a coordinated launch.</p>
      <h2>Proposed release rehearsal</h2>
      <p>With staff accounts, postpone the release, restrict one destination and sell out one variant before the queued announcement. Check that a recent purchaser does not receive another acquisition offer. Report eligible reach, purchases and unresolved waitlist demand separately; this rehearsal is proposed, not a launch result.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
